<title>UK: Whitbread sells Keg restaurant business.</title>
<headline>Whitbread sells Keg restaurant business.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brewer-to-leisure group Whitbread Plc said on Friday that it has agreed the sale of its Keg restaurant business to Canadian-based Raleigh Corp.</p>
<p>It said the deal, worth 23 million stg, is expected to be completed in April.  </p>
<p>Keg operates 63 managed and 18 franchised restaurants in Canada and the Pacific North West United States.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm delighted that we have reached an agreement to sell the Keg, which is non-core to Whitbread. Now is a good time for us to sell the business as it is producing sales growth and trading more profitably,&quot; said David Thomas, chief executive designate of Whitbread.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
